{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018AFxGWqb1DuHtXXYTCksxn","type":"tool_result","content":"## Iteration US-173 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config (ID: US-173)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/vercel.json` with Next.js framework configuration and environment variables:\r\n  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT (default: \"book-now\") for local development fallback\r\n  - EDGE_CONFIG placeholder for production Vercel Edge Config connection\r\n- Verified complete A/B testing implementation already in place:\r\n  - `flags.ts`: Flag types (CTAVariant with 3 options) and getVariant() function\r\n  - `proxy.ts`: Server-side flag evaluation in Next.js 16 proxy (formerly middleware)\r\n  - `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`: Reads variant from response headers (zero layout shift)\r\n  - `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx`: GA4 custom dimension (dimension_1) records variant for statistical analysis\r\n- Updated `.env.local` with NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT environment variable\r\n- Verified build passes: all 68+ static pages generated successfully\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js 16 uses `proxy()` function instead of middleware.ts (both cannot coexist in same project)\r\n- `proxy.ts` already had A/B testing logic in place but vercel.json was missing\r\n- Previous attempt failed with 12854-line oversized diff due to unrelated file modifications\r\n- This iteration focused on minimal required configuration: vercel.json + env setup verification\r\n- All acceptance criteria were already implemented by prior work; this iteration completes the story by adding the missing vercel.json configuration\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Vercel Flags UI in dashboard requires EDGE_CONFIG environment variable to be set in Vercel project settings\r\n- .env.local should NOT be committed (already in .gitignore); only .env.local.example and vercel.json are version-controlled\r\n- Next.js 16 proxy() is the evolution of middleware.ts; cannot have both files in src/ root\r\n- Flag values must be evaluated server-side in proxy() or middleware to prevent client-side flicker\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-162 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup (ID: US-162)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `lib/cache-utils.ts` with two functions:\r\n  - `getCachedData()`: Generic utility that wraps fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\r\n  - `getCachedRoomAvailability()`: Example implementation for room availability API calls\r\n- Updated `Rooms.tsx` Server Component to import and demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\r\n- Added try-catch error handling to gracefully handle AbortError when cache is invalidated\r\n- No TypeScript errors; all 83 pages generated successfully during build\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- React 19.2 cacheSignal() is only available in Server Components (not Client Components or Route Handlers)\r\n- cacheSignal() returns an AbortSignal that fires when cache lifetime ends\r\n- Pattern: `const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))`\r\n- AbortError has name property that can be checked to distinguish cache invalidation from network errors\r\n- Graceful error handling prevents cache-related aborts from breaking the page\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- cacheSignal() is a React 19.2 feature; requires Next.js 16+ for full support\r\n- Must import both `cache` and `cacheSignal` from \"react\" (not from \"next/cache\")\r\n- External API calls may fail during SSR (expected for example APIs) — always wrap in try-catch\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-161 (Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Replaced `useCallback` with `useEffectEvent` in RoomsEcommerceTracker.tsx and BookEcommerceTracker.tsx\r\n- Removed analytics click handlers from useEffect dependency arrays\r\n- Effects now run once on mount, not on every callback identity change\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Code was already committed in attempt 2 (d9fa754) but diff guard failed due to unstaged files inflating diff count\r\n- Attempt 3 only needed to verify code was in place and mark passes: true\r\n- When prior attempts commit code but fail post-commit gates, verify existing commits before re-implementing\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- SPIRAL diff guard counts ALL staged/unstaged changes, not just story-related files — always use `git add <specific-files>` not `git add -A`\r\n- Previous attempts failed at 540 and 23068 lines because unrelated modified files were included in the diff measurement\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-144 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Replace JavaScript tooltip positioning with CSS Popover API and Anchor Positioning (ID: US-144)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `InfoPopover.tsx` component using native HTML `popover` attribute, `popoverTarget`, CSS `anchor-name`/`position-anchor`\r\n- Added popover + anchor positioning CSS in globals.css with `@supports` fallback for browsers without anchor positioning\r\n- Converted Header.tsx search button `title` tooltip to InfoPopover\r\n- Converted HeroTrustBadges.tsx trust badge buttons to InfoPopover with contextual content\r\n- No JS tooltip library existed to remove (no Popper.js/Floating UI in the project)\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- React 19 includes `popover` and `popoverTarget` in its type definitions — no `@ts-expect-error` needed\r\n- `CSS.escape()` is a browser API not available in Node.js SSR — use regex sanitization instead for `useId()` output\r\n- Attempt 1 failed with 17,788 line diff — caused by touching package-lock.json or similar large files\r\n- Keep implementation under 500 lines total insertions+deletions\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- `useId()` returns colon-wrapped strings like `:r0:` — must sanitize for CSS custom property names\r\n- Linter may auto-revert changes if import is added separately from usage\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-143 (FINAL - Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (ID: US-143)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Added @starting-style CSS utility classes (.entry-fade, .entry-zoom-in, .entry-fade-up) to globals.css\r\n- Classes use only opacity + transform for GPU compositor thread\r\n- Includes prefers-reduced-motion: reduce override that disables transitions\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115e48ae-ae40-4acb-bf1e-0da935409628","uuid":"f6ba9681-51f4-4577-a35c-bbf4ab79b84b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T07:35:18.572Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Iteration US-173 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config (ID: US-173)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/vercel.json` with Next.js framework configuration and environment variables:\r\n  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT (default: \"book-now\") for local development fallback\r\n  - EDGE_CONFIG placeholder for production Vercel Edge Config connection\r\n- Verified complete A/B testing implementation already in place:\r\n  - `flags.ts`: Flag types (CTAVariant with 3 options) and getVariant() function\r\n  - `proxy.ts`: Server-side flag evaluation in Next.js 16 proxy (formerly middleware)\r\n  - `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`: Reads variant from response headers (zero layout shift)\r\n  - `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx`: GA4 custom dimension (dimension_1) records variant for statistical analysis\r\n- Updated `.env.local` with NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT environment variable\r\n- Verified build passes: all 68+ static pages generated successfully\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js 16 uses `proxy()` function instead of middleware.ts (both cannot coexist in same project)\r\n- `proxy.ts` already had A/B testing logic in place but vercel.json was missing\r\n- Previous attempt failed with 12854-line oversized diff due to unrelated file modifications\r\n- This iteration focused on minimal required configuration: vercel.json + env setup verification\r\n- All acceptance criteria were already implemented by prior work; this iteration completes the story by adding the missing vercel.json configuration\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Vercel Flags UI in dashboard requires EDGE_CONFIG environment variable to be set in Vercel project settings\r\n- .env.local should NOT be committed (already in .gitignore); only .env.local.example and vercel.json are version-controlled\r\n- Next.js 16 proxy() is the evolution of middleware.ts; cannot have both files in src/ root\r\n- Flag values must be evaluated server-side in proxy() or middleware to prevent client-side flicker\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-162 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup (ID: US-162)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `lib/cache-utils.ts` with two functions:\r\n  - `getCachedData()`: Generic utility that wraps fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\r\n  - `getCachedRoomAvailability()`: Example implementation for room availability API calls\r\n- Updated `Rooms.tsx` Server Component to import and demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\r\n- Added try-catch error handling to gracefully handle AbortError when cache is invalidated\r\n- No TypeScript errors; all 83 pages generated successfully during build\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- React 19.2 cacheSignal() is only available in Server Components (not Client Components or Route Handlers)\r\n- cacheSignal() returns an AbortSignal that fires when cache lifetime ends\r\n- Pattern: `const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))`\r\n- AbortError has name property that can be checked to distinguish cache invalidation from network errors\r\n- Graceful error handling prevents cache-related aborts from breaking the page\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- cacheSignal() is a React 19.2 feature; requires Next.js 16+ for full support\r\n- Must import both `cache` and `cacheSignal` from \"react\" (not from \"next/cache\")\r\n- External API calls may fail during SSR (expected for example APIs) — always wrap in try-catch\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-161 (Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Implement React 19.2 useEffectEvent for stable analytics event handlers (ID: US-161)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Replaced `useCallback` with `useEffectEvent` in RoomsEcommerceTracker.tsx and BookEcommerceTracker.tsx\r\n- Removed analytics click handlers from useEffect dependency arrays\r\n- Effects now run once on mount, not on every callback identity change\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Code was already committed in attempt 2 (d9fa754) but diff guard failed due to unstaged files inflating diff count\r\n- Attempt 3 only needed to verify code was in place and mark passes: true\r\n- When prior attempts commit code but fail post-commit gates, verify existing commits before re-implementing\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- SPIRAL diff guard counts ALL staged/unstaged changes, not just story-related files — always use `git add <specific-files>` not `git add -A`\r\n- Previous attempts failed at 540 and 23068 lines because unrelated modified files were included in the diff measurement\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-144 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Replace JavaScript tooltip positioning with CSS Popover API and Anchor Positioning (ID: US-144)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `InfoPopover.tsx` component using native HTML `popover` attribute, `popoverTarget`, CSS `anchor-name`/`position-anchor`\r\n- Added popover + anchor positioning CSS in globals.css with `@supports` fallback for browsers without anchor positioning\r\n- Converted Header.tsx search button `title` tooltip to InfoPopover\r\n- Converted HeroTrustBadges.tsx trust badge buttons to InfoPopover with contextual content\r\n- No JS tooltip library existed to remove (no Popper.js/Floating UI in the project)\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- React 19 includes `popover` and `popoverTarget` in its type definitions — no `@ts-expect-error` needed\r\n- `CSS.escape()` is a browser API not available in Node.js SSR — use regex sanitization instead for `useId()` output\r\n- Attempt 1 failed with 17,788 line diff — caused by touching package-lock.json or similar large files\r\n- Keep implementation under 500 lines total insertions+deletions\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- `useId()` returns colon-wrapped strings like `:r0:` — must sanitize for CSS custom property names\r\n- Linter may auto-revert changes if import is added separately from usage\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-143 (FINAL - Attempt 3) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations (ID: US-143)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Added @starting-style CSS utility classes (.entry-fade, .entry-zoom-in, .entry-fade-up) to globals.css\r\n- Classes use only opacity + transform for GPU compositor thread\r\n- Includes prefers-reduced-motion: reduce override that disables transitions","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
